==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|distincte}}, past participle of {{m|enm|distincten||to distinguish, discern}}, from {{der|en|fro|destincter}}, from {{der|en|la|distinctus}}, past participle of {{m|la|distinguere||to distinguish}}; see {{m|en|distinguish}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈstɪŋkt/|a=RP,GA,CA,AU}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-distinct.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/dəˈstəŋkt/|a=NZ}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪŋkt|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er,more}}

# Capable of being perceived very [[clear]]ly.
#: {{ux|en|Her voice was '''distinct''' despite the heavy traffic.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=July-August|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/fenella-saunders Fenella Saunders]
|title=[http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/tiny-lenses-see-the-big-picture Tiny Lenses See the Big Picture]|magazine=w:American Scientist
|passage=The single-imaging optic of the mammalian eye offers some '''distinct''' visual advantages. Such lenses can take in photons from a wide range of angles, increasing light sensitivity. They also have high spatial resolution, resolving incoming images in minute detail.}}
# [[different|Different]] from one another (with the preferable adposition being "[[from]]").
#: {{ux|en|Horses are '''distinct''' from zebras.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1928|author=Lawrence R. Bourne| title=Well Tackled!| chapter=13| url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5387037W| passage=“Yes, there are two '''distinct''' sets of footprints, both wearing rubber shoes—one I think ordinary plimsolls, the other goloshes,” replied the sergeant.}}
# [[noticeably|Noticeably]] [[different]] from others; [[distinctive]].
#: {{ux|en|Olga's voice is quite '''distinct''' because of her accent.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:CBC News|title=Basque group ETA declares end to violent campaign|date=October 20 2011|author=w:Associated Press
|text=The Basque country is a small but wealthy and verdant region of northern Spain, with its own '''distinct''' culture and an ancient language that linguists cannot trace and sounds nothing like Spanish.
|url=https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/basque-group-eta-declares-end-to-violent-campaign-1.1107657
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250716092119/https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/basque-group-eta-declares-end-to-violent-campaign-1.1107657}}
# Separate in place; not conjunct or united; with ''from''.
#* {{RQ:Clarendon History|passage=The intention was that the two armies which marched out together should afterward be '''distinct'''.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[distinguished|Distinguished]]; having the difference marked; separated by a visible sign; [[marked out]]; [[specified]].
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=7|passage=Wherever thus created &mdash; for no place / Is yet '''distinct''' by name.|year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[marked|Marked]]; [[variegated]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=VI|canto=III|stanza=23|passage=The which [place] was dight / With divers flowres '''distinct''' with rare delight.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|capable of being perceived very clearly}} {{l|en|clear}}, {{l|en|vivid}}; see also [[Thesaurus:distinct]]
* {{sense|different from one another}} {{l|en|different}}, {{l|en|separate}}, {{l|en|several}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}
* {{sense|noticeably different}} {{l|en|characteristic}}, {{l|en|distinctive}}, {{l|en|prominent}}
* {{sense|separate in place}} {{l|en|discrete}}, {{l|en|individual}}, {{l|en|noncontinuous}}, {{l|en|separate}}
* {{sense|distinguished}} {{l|en|specified}}
* {{sense|marked}} {{l|en|patterned}}; see also [[Thesaurus:marked]]

====Antonyms====
* {{antsense|capable of being perceived very clearly}} {{l|en|confusing}}, {{l|en|indistinct}}; see also [[Thesaurus:indistinct]]
* {{antsense|different from one another}} {{l|en|same}}, {{l|en|indistinguishable}}

