# {{senseid|en|respect}} {{lb|en|sometimes|proscribed}}<ref name=GMEU5-sv-dignity>{{cite-book |en |year=2022 |last=Garner |first=Bryan A. |authorlink=Bryan A. Garner |entry=dignity |title=w:Garner's Modern English Usage |edition=5 |publisher=Oxford University Press |isbn=9780197599020}}</ref> {{1|respect}}.&nbsp;{{tea room sense|en|m=December|y=2025}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Speeches of Edward, Lord Lytton Now First Collected. With Some of His Political Writings Hitherto Unpublished|volume=13|year_published=1874|author=w:Edward Bulwer-Lytton|year=''a''. 1873|page=xl|pageurl=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Speeches_of_Edward_Lord_Lytton_Now_First/uPA4AQAAIAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22treat%7Ctreats%7Ctreating%7Ctreated%22++%22with+dignity%22&pg=PR40&printsec=frontcover|chapter=Prefatory Memoir|text=That in such an undertaking, if put on its right footing, and treated with '''dignity''' by the State, you would have the cheerful assistance of the first scientific teachers who have turned their philosophy to such practical uses, I have no doubt.}}
